# RFC-0002: CQRS

Status: Active

## Abstract

Every use case in `Raytha.Application` is one file containing a static outer
class with nested `Command` or `Query`, `Validator`, and `Handler` types,
dispatched through Mediator (source-generated, `ISender`).

## 1. File Shape

- One use case per file, named after the outer class: `CreateUser.cs`,
  `GetContentItems.cs`.
- Commands live in `<Feature>/Commands/`, queries in `<Feature>/Queries/`.
  Namespace matches the folder (`Raytha.Application.Users.Commands`).
- The outer type MUST be a plain class used only as a namespace for the nested
  types. It MUST NOT hold state or logic.

```csharp
public class CreateUser
{
    public record Command : LoggableRequest<CommandResponseDto<ShortGuid>> { }
    public class Validator : AbstractValidator<Command> { }
    public class Handler : IRequestHandler<Command, CommandResponseDto<ShortGuid>> { }
}
```

## 2. Commands

- Commands MUST be `record` types with `init`-only properties.
- Commands MUST derive from `LoggableRequest<T>` or `LoggableEntityRequest<T>`
  so `AuditBehavior` writes an audit row. `ApplicationConventionTests` fails
  any new `Command` that does not — the exemption list in that test is closed to
  new entries without a stated reason.
- Commands return `CommandResponseDto<T>`, usually `CommandResponseDto<ShortGuid>`
  for the affected id.
- A command that should fire a webhook carries `[WebhookEvent("resource.action")]`
  (RFC-0011).

## 3. Queries

- Queries MUST be read-only. A query handler MUST NOT call `SaveChangesAsync`.
- Single-entity queries take `GetEntityByIdInputDto`; list queries derive from
  `GetPagedEntitiesInputDto` (`PageNumber`, `PageSize`, `Search`, `OrderBy`).
- Queries return `QueryResponseDto<T>`, with `ListResultDto<T>` for pages.
- Each list query owns its default ordering and its allowlist of sortable
  columns. An unknown `OrderBy` MUST fall back to that default rather than
  reaching the database as raw SQL.

## 4. Validators

- Input validation is FluentValidation only, in the nested `Validator`.
  `ValidationBehavior` runs it before the handler, so handlers MUST NOT
  re-validate shape.
- A validator MAY inject `IRaythaDbContext` for uniqueness and existence
  checks. Keep those reads cheap.
- Validators MUST NOT mutate state or send email.

## 5. Handlers

- Handlers implement `IRequestHandler<TRequest, TResponse>` and return
  `ValueTask<TResponse>` (Mediator, not MediatR).
- Handlers take dependencies through the constructor as interfaces from
  `Common/Interfaces`. A handler MUST NOT resolve services from a container or
  reach for `HttpContext`.
- One `SaveChangesAsync` per command handler. Work that must succeed together
  goes in one call; work that may lag (email, webhooks, indexing) goes to a
  background task via `IBackgroundTaskQueue`.
- Handlers MUST NOT call another handler through `ISender`. Extract the shared
  logic instead.
- Handlers throw `NotFoundException` / `ForbiddenAccessException` from
  `Common/Exceptions` for missing or unauthorized entities. Do not return a
  success DTO describing a failure.

## 6. Pipeline

`AddApplicationServices` registers behaviors in order: unhandled exception
logging, validation, audit, webhook publish. New behaviors MUST be registered
there and MUST be ordered deliberately — a behavior that runs after
`ValidationBehavior` never sees an invalid request.

## 7. Callers

- `Raytha.Web` calls use cases only through `ISender`. Controllers, Razor pages,
  and minimal-API endpoints MUST NOT touch `IRaythaDbContext` (RFC-0004).
- Background tasks implement `IExecuteBackgroundTask` and MUST be registered in
  `AddApplicationServices`; `ApplicationConventionTests` enforces it, because an
  unregistered task fails only when first dequeued.
